 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study did not find a speed and step-out combination that makes the 2 Hz VaVAM policy fail. Four of the five cases were confirmed, but all four are the nominal setting (1.0x, 0 s) on scenes that fail anyway: 048b974e, 07981e6a, 0d4893f5 and 1bbe02fc. Every failure analysed involved a parked car, a neighbouring car or the road edge. None involved the pedestrian. On 1bbe02fc the failures are borderline road-edge flags that may come from the map rather than the policy. No off-nominal setting failed. Those settings mostly ran once each, only between 0.6x and 1.2x and at shifts of \u22120.5 s or 0 s, so this says little about the rest of the grid.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 048b974e the policy fails at the nominal setting by leaving the route at the intersection and driving its front into a parked van or car at the curb. The runs are flagged as possible artifacts because the ego was far off the recorded path, but the video review blames the policy's wrong turn, not rendering.",
    "settings": [
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 07981e6a the policy fails at the nominal setting. It ignores the RIGHT command, drifts left into the parked cars at about 10\u201311 m/s and barely brakes.",
    "settings": [
     "S2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 0d4893f5 the policy fails at the nominal setting. It drifts left into the next lane and hits the car travelling alongside it without braking. This is a sideways drift, not a failure to stop for the car ahead.",
    "settings": [
     "S11"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 1bbe02fc every failure at the nominal setting is a road-edge flag at the stop line, with the ego under 1 m from where the human drove. The video review could not say whether the policy was at fault, so this confirmed case may be a map-edge artifact.",
    "settings": [
     "S27"
    ]
